      "writtenOn": "2025-06-06T15:46:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need to apply OOTF for PQ2 and HLG2, right?  IIUC from the skcms changes, the actual number of parameters we require won\u0027t change because we can assume constants for a number of parameters that we allow to change for PQ-ish and HLG-ish.\n\nInstead of adding 2 more float4\u0027s, can we preemptively add branches in the above/below encode/linear cases for PQ2 and HLG2.  We already have negative numbers to differentiate PQish and HLGish from sRGBish so it\u0027ll be easy to have something like:\n```\n   else if (srcGABC.x \u003c -3) {\n       colorF \u003d sign(colorF) J* $apply_pq_xfer_fn(abs(colorF), constants for PQ2);\n       colorF \u003d $apply_ootf(colorF, re-interpret srcGABC/DEF as needed);\n   } else if (srcGABC.x \u003c -2) {\n       as above buyt for explicit HLG + $apply_ootf call\n   }\n```\n and we have that for the dst case as well?",
